Subject: [PATCH] Honor the driver's sysinput activation capability

The donor Touch class unconditionally enables the state,early activation
protocol. SM8250's driver reports support_feature=269 (0x10d), without
SUPPORT_SYSINPUT_ENABLED (0x20), and retains the boolean input/enabled path.
InputReader already uses that feature mask to select the legacy power path.

Use the reported bit for Touch.supportActivate as well, so the newer HAL
does not duplicate legacy power handling or write a nonexistent enabled node.
Keep all touch commands/properties and the working legacy power path intact.
Drivers that advertise 0x20 continue using HAL activation.

--- a/smali/com/samsung/android/hardware/secinputdev/device/Touch.smali
+++ b/smali/com/samsung/android/hardware/secinputdev/device/Touch.smali
@@ -438,7 +438,18 @@
 .method protected supportActivate()Z
     .locals 1
 
+    iget v0, p0, Lcom/samsung/android/hardware/secinputdev/device/SemInputDevice;->supportFeature:I
+
+    and-int/lit8 v0, v0, 0x20
+
+    if-eqz v0, :legacy_power_control
+
     const/4 v0, 0x1
 
     return v0
+
+    :legacy_power_control
+    const/4 v0, 0x0
+
+    return v0
 .end method
